== Allomorphy ==
These various changes, especially syncope, produced quite complex [[allomorphy]], because the addition of prefixes or various pre-verbal particles ([[proclitic]]s) in Proto-Celtic changed the syllable containing the stress: According to the Celtic variant of [[Clitic#Word order|Wackernagel's law]], the stress fell on the second syllable of the verbal complex, including any prefixes and clitics. By the Old Irish period, most of this allomorphy still remained, although it was rapidly eliminated beginning in the Middle Irish period.

Among the most striking changes are in prefixed verbs with or without pre-verbal particles. With a single prefix and without a proclitic, stress falls on the verbal root, which assumes the ''deuterotonic'' ("second-stressed") form. With a prefix and also with a proclitic, stress falls on the prefix, and the verb assumes the ''prototonic'' ("first-stressed") form. Rather extreme allomorphic differences can result:

